# Fallback on-screen keyboard policy (task 014 P2b), end to end with APPLAUNCH_OSK=auto (the normal rule) and the
# harness' presence fixture ("keyboards N"): Settings > System > On-screen keyboard Off: the Keyboard test field
# edits without a keyboard; set back to Auto through its choice list: the keyboard shows; a physical keyboard
# appears: it goes within the policy poll (250 ms). Review only, no golden.
title on-screen keyboard policy
review
sizes 640x480 800x480
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 1
env APPLAUNCH_OSK auto
config osk_mode 1
keyboards 0
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
launch Settings
key UP
key ENTER
key UP
key UP
key UP
key UP
shot osk_policy_setting_off
key DOWN
key ENTER
shot osk_policy_off
# Esc stops editing, Esc again leaves the form; the choice list: Off is checked, Up then Enter picks Auto
key ESC
key ESC
key UP
key ENTER
key UP
key ENTER
shot osk_policy_setting_auto
key DOWN
key ENTER
shot osk_policy_auto
keyboards 1
wait 400
shot osk_policy_keyboard_appeared
